        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a.  $ \\underline{\\text{Duty Station}} $. The Transport Unit maintains offices throughout the State of Oregon. The employee's assigned office will be determined at the time of hire.",
            "block_bbox": [
                104,
                109,
                1117,
                160
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 0,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    104.0,
                    109.0
                ],
                [
                    1117.0,
                    109.0
                ],
                [
                    1117.0,
                    160.0
                ],
                [
                    104.0,
                    160.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b. Overnight Travel. For the purpose of escorting inmates to and from the state of Oregon the agency will first seek volunteers using the out-of-state list. If no employee volunteers the employee at the top of the out-of-state list will be assigned the trip. Assigned staff may be flexed to accommodate flight schedules.",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                160,
                1118,
                259
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    160.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    160.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    259.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    259.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "When assigned duties requiring overnight travel, there will be no out of pocket expenses incurred by employees. Covered expenses will be in accordance with the Department of Administrative Services travel policy and distributed by cash advance. Unforeseen covered expenses will be processed for reimbursement at the completion of the duty assianment.",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                260,
                1118,
                361
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    102.35803985595703,
                    267.0044860839844
                ],
                [
                    1117.0,
                    260.0000305175781
                ],
                [
                    1117.6419677734375,
                    352.9955749511719
                ],
                [
                    103.00000762939453,
                    360.0000305175781
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If return travel plans are delayed due to circumstances beyond the control of the agency, the employee will be considered on-call. There will be an eight (8) hour break between the end of one (1) days and the beginning of the next workday except in emergencies, or unforeseen circumstances. This will be in accordance with the restrictions of Article 19 of this collective bargaining agreement. The employee has the option of receiving compensatory time equal to their regularly scheduled shift in lieu of the on-call pay.",
            "block_bbox": [
                104,
                361,
                1119,
                511
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    104.0,
                    361.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    361.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    511.0
                ],
                [
                    104.0,
                    511.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "c. Schedule Bidding. Due to variable start times and operational needs of the separate offices, each office retains the right to operate with or without a bid system. Employees assigned to Transportation can bid their regular start time and days off in order of seniority. Seniority, for the purpose of bidding will be calculated by time in classification and with the Department of Corrections. The Agency will post start time and day off schedules thirty (30) calendar days before the rotation date. Employees will have ten (10) working days following the posting of the work schedules to submit their bids. Selections will be submitted in priority order. Employees who do not submit a bid will be assigned by the agency.",
            "block_bbox": [
                105,
                513,
                1118,
                713
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    105.0,
                    513.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    513.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    713.0
                ],
                [
                    105.0,
                    713.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Schedule bidding and rotations will occur every six (6) months effective on the first Sunday in July and January.",
            "block_bbox": [
